#
# Rows appended to woof-CE's DISTRO_PKGS_SPECS table by build.sh, before 0setup.
# Format: yes|<generic name>|<comma-separated distro packages>|<splits>||deps:yes
# No comments inside the table: 0setup reads it as a shell list of pipe-separated rows, so the "why" for
# each row lives here, above the blank line, and nowhere else.
#
# Measured 2026-11-02 on the resolute64 rootfs (build root sandbox3/rootfs-complete, 1.5 GB) that the merged
# package set does NOT carry, and that TPUPPY-RELEASE needs:
#   U1  sudo            - absent from the rootfs and from the table entirely
#   U1  apt             - absent; libapt-pkg7.0 only arrives as a dependency of xserver_xorg, so `apt` is
#                         a missing binary, not a missing library ("sh: sudo: not found" on c20 was this
#                         class of gap)
#   U4  mokutil         - absent; the release check's Secure Boot row needs it to read the state
#   U7  openssh-server  - absent (only openssh-client has a row), so the stick cannot be checked over ssh
#
#   U6  fdisk           - measured on the built rootfs: /usr/sbin/fdisk is there and /usr/sbin/sfdisk is
#                         NOT, so 1bit-install cannot write a GPT (the 26.04 split ships both in the fdisk
#                         package; the file that survives woof-CE's splitting is the one with a spec row)
#
# bash, dpkg, python3, efibootmgr, jwm, rox, xterm and curl are already in the merged set (measured).

yes|apt|apt|exe,dev>null,doc>null,nls>null||deps:yes
yes|sudo|sudo|exe,dev>null,doc>null,nls>null||deps:yes
yes|mokutil|mokutil|exe,dev>null,doc>null,nls>null||deps:yes
yes|openssh-server|openssh-server|exe,dev>null,doc>null,nls>null||deps:yes
yes|fdisk|fdisk|exe,dev>null,doc>null,nls>null||deps:yes
